            "body": "Monsoon ki shaam thi. **Akash** apni balcony mein ek chhota sa rectangular wire frame haath mein liye khada tha. Baarish seedhi neeche gir rahi thi. Jab usne frame ko bilkul horizontal (flat) rakha, to zyada se zyada boondein uske andar se guzri. Jab usne frame ko thoda tirchha (tilt) kiya, to kam boondein andar se nikli. Aur jab usne frame ko bilkul vertical khada kar diya — boondon ke parallel — to ek bhi boond frame ke paar nahi gayi!\n\nPapa ne chai peete hue muskurakar kaha: \"Akash, physics mein electric field ke saath bhi bilkul yahi hota hai. Kisi surface ke paar kitni electric field lines guzar rahi hain, use **Electric Flux** kehte hain — aur isse humein Electrostatics ka sabse kamaal ka shortcut milta hai: **Gauss's Law**!\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Monsoon ki shaam thi. **Akash** apni balcony mein ek chhota sa rectangular wire frame haath mein liye khada tha. Baarish seedhi neeche gir rahi thi. Jab usne frame ko bilkul horizontal (flat) rakha, to zyada se zyada boondein uske andar se guzri. Jab usne frame ko thoda tirchha (tilt) kiya, to kam boondein andar se nikli. Aur jab usne frame ko bilkul vertical khada kar diya — boondon ke parallel — to ek bhi boond frame ke paar nahi gayi!\n\nPapa ne chai peete hue muskurakar kaha: \"Akash, physics mein electric field ke saath bhi bilkul yahi hota hai. Kisi surface ke paar kitni electric field lines guzar rahi hain, use **Electric Flux** kehte hain — aur isse humein Electrostatics ka sabse kamaal ka shortcut milta hai: **Gauss's Law**!\""
