            "headingHinglish": "Naye Shabd (New Words)",
            "body": "- **EMF (Electromotive Force, ε):** Jab cell se **koi current nahi liya ja raha (open circuit)**, tab uske dono terminals ke beech ka maximum potential difference. Naam mein \"force\" hai, par yeh force nahi — **work done per unit charge** hai! SI unit **Volt (V)**.\n- **Internal Resistance (r):** Cell ke andar maujood electrolyte aur electrodes dwara current ke raaste mein lagayi jaane wali rukawat (unit **Ω**).\n- **Terminal Potential Difference (V):** Jab cell circuit mein current de raha ho (ya charge ho raha ho), tab uske dono terminals ke beech actual voltage.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **EMF (Electromotive Force, ε):** Jab cell se **koi current nahi liya ja raha (open circuit)**, tab uske dono terminals ke beech ka maximum potential difference. Naam mein \"force\" hai, par yeh force nahi — **work done per unit charge** hai! SI unit **Volt (V)**.\n- **Internal Resistance (r):** Cell ke andar maujood electrolyte aur electrodes dwara current ke raaste mein lagayi jaane wali rukawat (unit **Ω**).\n- **Terminal Potential Difference (V):** Jab cell circuit mein current de raha ho (ya charge ho raha ho), tab uske dono terminals ke beech actual voltage."
