            "body": "Class mein **Nidhi** ek charging parallel-plate capacitor ka diagram dekh rahi thi. Wire mein conduction current **I** beh raha tha, aur uske paas ek compass deflect ho raha tha. Par jab teacher ma'am ne bataya ki capacitor ki dono plates ke beech ke **khali air gap** mein bhi bilkul wahi magnetic field hota hai, to Nidhi chaunk gayi: \"Ma'am, dono plates ke beech to hawa (insulator) hai — koi electron jump karke paar nahi ja raha! Phir wahan current I = 0 hone ke baawajood magnetic field kaise ban gaya?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am muskurayi: \"1864 mein James Clerk Maxwell ke dimaag mein bhi bilkul yahi sawaal aaya tha — aur iske jawaab ne physics ki duniya badal di! Maxwell ne kaha ki badalta hua **Electric Flux** bhi bilkul current ki tarah magnetic field paida karta hai — isse **Displacement Current** kehte hain!\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Class mein **Nidhi** ek charging parallel-plate capacitor ka diagram dekh rahi thi. Wire mein conduction current **I** beh raha tha, aur uske paas ek compass deflect ho raha tha. Par jab teacher ma'am ne bataya ki capacitor ki dono plates ke beech ke **khali air gap** mein bhi bilkul wahi magnetic field hota hai, to Nidhi chaunk gayi: \"Ma'am, dono plates ke beech to hawa (insulator) hai — koi electron jump karke paar nahi ja raha! Phir wahan current I = 0 hone ke baawajood magnetic field kaise ban gaya?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am muskurayi: \"1864 mein James Clerk Maxwell ke dimaag mein bhi bilkul yahi sawaal aaya tha — aur iske jawaab ne physics ki duniya badal di! Maxwell ne kaha ki badalta hua **Electric Flux** bhi bilkul current ki tarah magnetic field paida karta hai — isse **Displacement Current** kehte hain!\""
