            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "| Concept | Key Fact / Formula |\n|---|---|\n| Wavefront & Ray | Constant-phase surface; Rays are ALWAYS **⊥** to wavefronts |\n| Shapes | Point source → Spherical; Line source → Cylindrical; Distant source → Plane |\n| Huygens' Principle | Every point on wavefront emits secondary wavelets; forward envelope = new wavefront |\n| Refraction by Wavefronts | sin i / sin r = v₁ / v₂ = n₂ / n₁; **f constant**, v = c/n, λ' = λ/n |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Concept | Key Fact / Formula |\n|---|---|\n| Wavefront & Ray | Constant-phase surface; Rays are ALWAYS **⊥** to wavefronts |\n| Shapes | Point source → Spherical; Line source → Cylindrical; Distant source → Plane |\n| Huygens' Principle | Every point on wavefront emits secondary wavelets; forward envelope = new wavefront |\n| Refraction by Wavefronts | sin i / sin r = v₁ / v₂ = n₂ / n₁; **f constant**, v = c/n, λ' = λ/n |"
