          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. Define (a) work function of a metal, (b) threshold frequency, and (c) stopping potential.\n2. Why are alkali metals like Caesium and Potassium commonly used as photosensitive materials in photocells?\n3. State three experimental observations of the photoelectric effect that cannot be explained by classical wave theory of light.\n4. The maximum kinetic energy of photoelectrons emitted from a metal surface is 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the stopping potential V₀ in Volts.\n5. If the stopping potential in a photoelectric experiment is 2.5 V, what is the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in eV and in Joules?\n6. How does the saturation photocurrent change when the distance between a point light source and the photocell is halved (keeping frequency ν > ν₀ constant)? (Hint: intensity I ∝ 1/r²!)\n7. What happens to the stopping potential in Question 6 when the point light source is brought closer?\n8. Name the three main ways to emit free electrons from a metal surface.\n9. State whether True or False: If light of frequency less than the threshold frequency ν₀ shines on a metal for a very long time, photoelectrons will eventually be emitted.\n10. Two metals A and B have work functions 2.2 eV and 4.5 eV respectively. Which metal has the higher threshold frequency ν₀?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (a) **Work function (φ₀):** Metal satah se ek electron bahar nikaalne ki minimum energy.\n   (b) **Threshold frequency (ν₀):** Minimum frequency jiske bina photoelectric emission nahi hota.\n   (c) **Stopping potential (V₀):** Minimum negative collector voltage jo photocurrent ko zero kar de (K_max = eV₀).\n\n2. Caesium aur Potassium ka **work function φ₀ bahut kam** (~2.1–2.3 eV) hota hai, isliye woh aam **visible light** se bhi aasaani se photoelectrons emit kar dete hain!\n\n3. (i) K_max intensity par depend nahi karti (wave theory kehti thi depend karni chahiye); (ii) Threshold frequency ν₀ ka hona (ν < ν₀ par zero emission); (iii) Emission ka instantaneous (< 10⁻⁹ s) hona (koi time lag nahi!).\n\n4. K_max = e V₀ ⟹ V₀ = (3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹) / (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = **2.0 V**.\n   Jaanch: 2.0 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ J ✅.\n\n5. **K_max = 2.5 eV** = 2.5 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = **4.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ J**.\n   Jaanch: 2.5 × 1.6 = 4.0 ✅.\n\n6. Doori r aadhi hone par intensity **I ∝ 1/r²** **4 guna (4 times)** badh jaati hai ⟹ **saturation photocurrent 4 guna** badh jayega!\n\n7. Stopping potential V₀ **bilkul nahi badlega (unchanged)**, kyunki V₀ sirf frequency par depend karta hai, intensity par nahi!\n\n8. (i) **Thermionic emission** (heating), (ii) **Field emission** (strong electric field), (iii) **Photoelectric emission** (light).\n\n9. **False ❌.** Agar ν < ν₀ ho, to chahe kitni hi der ya kitni hi bright light daalo, **kabhi koi electron nahi nikalta**!\n\n10. **Metal B (4.5 eV)** ki threshold frequency ν₀ zyada hogi (kyunki φ₀ = h ν₀ ⟹ zyada work function = zyada threshold frequency)!\n\n---\n\nAb tum Photoelectric Effect ke saare experimental observations aur wave theory ki haar samajh chuke ho!\n\n**Agle topic mein:** 1905 mein **Albert Einstein** ne is rahasya ko sirf 1 equation se kaise suljhaya — **Photons** aur **Einstein's Photoelectric Equation** seekhenge!",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. Define (a) work function of a metal, (b) threshold frequency, and (c) stopping potential.\n2. Why are alkali metals like Caesium and Potassium commonly used as photosensitive materials in photocells?\n3. State three experimental observations of the photoelectric effect that cannot be explained by classical wave theory of light.\n4. The maximum kinetic energy of photoelectrons emitted from a metal surface is 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the stopping potential V₀ in Volts.\n5. If the stopping potential in a photoelectric experiment is 2.5 V, what is the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in eV and in Joules?\n6. How does the saturation photocurrent change when the distance between a point light source and the photocell is halved (keeping frequency ν > ν₀ constant)? (Hint: intensity I ∝ 1/r²!)\n7. What happens to the stopping potential in Question 6 when the point light source is brought closer?\n8. Name the three main ways to emit free electrons from a metal surface.\n9. State whether True or False: If light of frequency less than the threshold frequency ν₀ shines on a metal for a very long time, photoelectrons will eventually be emitted.\n10. Two metals A and B have work functions 2.2 eV and 4.5 eV respectively. Which metal has the higher threshold frequency ν₀?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (a) **Work function (φ₀):** Metal satah se ek electron bahar nikaalne ki minimum energy.\n   (b) **Threshold frequency (ν₀):** Minimum frequency jiske bina photoelectric emission nahi hota.\n   (c) **Stopping potential (V₀):** Minimum negative collector voltage jo photocurrent ko zero kar de (K_max = eV₀).\n\n2. Caesium aur Potassium ka **work function φ₀ bahut kam** (~2.1–2.3 eV) hota hai, isliye woh aam **visible light** se bhi aasaani se photoelectrons emit kar dete hain!\n\n3. (i) K_max intensity par depend nahi karti (wave theory kehti thi depend karni chahiye); (ii) Threshold frequency ν₀ ka hona (ν < ν₀ par zero emission); (iii) Emission ka instantaneous (< 10⁻⁹ s) hona (koi time lag nahi!).\n\n4. K_max = e V₀ ⟹ V₀ = (3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹) / (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = **2.0 V**.\n   Jaanch: 2.0 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ J ✅.\n\n5. **K_max = 2.5 eV** = 2.5 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = **4.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ J**.\n   Jaanch: 2.5 × 1.6 = 4.0 ✅.\n\n6. Doori r aadhi hone par intensity **I ∝ 1/r²** **4 guna (4 times)** badh jaati hai ⟹ **saturation photocurrent 4 guna** badh jayega!\n\n7. Stopping potential V₀ **bilkul nahi badlega (unchanged)**, kyunki V₀ sirf frequency par depend karta hai, intensity par nahi!\n\n8. (i) **Thermionic emission** (heating), (ii) **Field emission** (strong electric field), (iii) **Photoelectric emission** (light).\n\n9. **False ❌.** Agar ν < ν₀ ho, to chahe kitni hi der ya kitni hi bright light daalo, **kabhi koi electron nahi nikalta**!\n\n10. **Metal B (4.5 eV)** ki threshold frequency ν₀ zyada hogi (kyunki φ₀ = h ν₀ ⟹ zyada work function = zyada threshold frequency)!\n\n---\n\nAb tum Photoelectric Effect ke saare experimental observations aur wave theory ki haar samajh chuke ho!\n\n**Agle topic mein:** 1905 mein **Albert Einstein** ne is rahasya ko sirf 1 equation se kaise suljhaya — **Photons** aur **Einstein's Photoelectric Equation** seekhenge!"
          }
