            "body": "Physics club ke quiz mein **Reema** ko ek ajeeb paheli mili: \"Ek sodium metal plate par 1000-watt ki super-bright **red** spotlight daali gayi — ek bhi electron nahi nikla! Phir ek chhoti si 1-watt ki dim **violet** torch daali gayi — aur turant electrons nikalne lage! Aisa kaise hua?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am muskurayi: \"1905 mein **Albert Einstein** ne iska jawaab diya — jis par unhe **Nobel Prize** mila! Einstein ne kaha ki light continuous wave ki tarah nahi, balki chhote-chhote energy packets (**Photons / Quanta**) ke roop mein aati hai! Ek red photon mein electron ko bahar nikaalne layak energy nahi hoti, jabki ek akela violet photon kaafi energy lekar aata hai!\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Physics club ke quiz mein **Reema** ko ek ajeeb paheli mili: \"Ek sodium metal plate par 1000-watt ki super-bright **red** spotlight daali gayi — ek bhi electron nahi nikla! Phir ek chhoti si 1-watt ki dim **violet** torch daali gayi — aur turant electrons nikalne lage! Aisa kaise hua?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am muskurayi: \"1905 mein **Albert Einstein** ne iska jawaab diya — jis par unhe **Nobel Prize** mila! Einstein ne kaha ki light continuous wave ki tarah nahi, balki chhote-chhote energy packets (**Photons / Quanta**) ke roop mein aati hai! Ek red photon mein electron ko bahar nikaalne layak energy nahi hoti, jabki ek akela violet photon kaafi energy lekar aata hai!\""
