            "body": "Biology magazine mein **Rina** ne ek nanhe virus ki super-sharp 3D photo dekhi jiske neeche likha tha: *\"Captured with an Electron Microscope — 100× sharper than any light microscope!\"* Rina ne socha: \"Light microscope ki limit light ki wavelength (400 nm) se hoti hai — par Electron Microscope mein to **electrons** (particles!) bheje jaate hain! Electrons ki apni wavelength kaise ho sakti hai?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am boli: \"1924 mein Louis **de Broglie** ne ek brilliant symmetry sochi: *Nature symmetry pasand karti hai! Agar Light (wave) kabhi Particle (photon) ban sakti hai, to har chalta hua Particle (electron, proton, even cricket ball!) bhi ek **Wave (Matter Wave)** ki tarah behave karta hai!*\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Biology magazine mein **Rina** ne ek nanhe virus ki super-sharp 3D photo dekhi jiske neeche likha tha: *\"Captured with an Electron Microscope — 100× sharper than any light microscope!\"* Rina ne socha: \"Light microscope ki limit light ki wavelength (400 nm) se hoti hai — par Electron Microscope mein to **electrons** (particles!) bheje jaate hain! Electrons ki apni wavelength kaise ho sakti hai?\"\n\nTeacher ma'am boli: \"1924 mein Louis **de Broglie** ne ek brilliant symmetry sochi: *Nature symmetry pasand karti hai! Agar Light (wave) kabhi Particle (photon) ban sakti hai, to har chalta hua Particle (electron, proton, even cricket ball!) bhi ek **Wave (Matter Wave)** ki tarah behave karta hai!*\""
