          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. State Bohr's three postulates for the Hydrogen atom.\n2. What is the physical significance of the negative sign in the total energy E_n = −13.6/n² eV of an electron in a Hydrogen atom?\n3. Calculate the radius of the (a) 3rd orbit (n = 3), and (b) 4th orbit (n = 4) of a Hydrogen atom (given a₀ = 0.53 Å).\n4. The total energy of an electron in the first excited state (n = 2) of Hydrogen is −3.4 eV. What are its kinetic energy and potential energy in this state?\n5. Find the ratio of speeds of an electron in the n = 1 and n = 3 orbits of a Hydrogen atom.\n6. Calculate the energy (in eV) of the photon emitted when an electron in Hydrogen jumps from n = 3 (−1.51 eV) to n = 2 (−3.40 eV).\n7. What is the ratio of the radii of the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Bohr orbits of Hydrogen?\n8. Calculate the ground-state (n = 1) total energy of a singly ionised Helium ion He⁺ (Z = 2) using E_n = −13.6 Z²/n² eV.\n9. State whether True or False: According to Bohr's model, an electron continuously radiates electromagnetic energy while revolving in a stationary orbit.\n10. If the kinetic energy of an electron in a Bohr orbit is +1.51 eV, find (a) its total energy, (b) its potential energy, and (c) the orbit number n (for Hydrogen).\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (i) Electron stationary circular orbits mein bina radiation chhode ghoomta hai; (ii) Angular momentum quantised hai: **L = n h / (2π)**; (iii) Jump karne par photon emit/absorb hota hai: **h ν = E_i − E_f**.\n\n2. Negative sign batata hai ki electron nucleus ke electrostatic attraction se **bandha (bound)** hua hai — use atom se poori tarah alag karne ke liye bahar se positive energy deni padegi!\n\n3. (a) r₃ = 0.53 × 3² = 0.53 × 9 = **4.77 Å**.\n   (b) r₄ = 0.53 × 4² = 0.53 × 16 = **8.48 Å**.\n   Jaanch: 0.53 × 9 = 4.77; 0.53 × 16 = 8.48 ✅.\n\n4. **K = −E = +3.4 eV**; **U = 2 E = −6.8 eV**.\n   Jaanch: +3.4 − 6.8 = −3.4 eV ✅.\n\n5. v_n ∝ 1 / n ⟹ **v₁ : v₃ = 3 : 1**.\n\n6. ΔE = E₃ − E₂ = −1.51 − (−3.40) = **1.89 eV**.\n   Jaanch: 3.40 − 1.51 = 1.89 eV ✅.\n\n7. r_n ∝ n² ⟹ r₁ : r₂ : r₃ = 1² : 2² : 3² = **1 : 4 : 9**.\n\n8. Z = 2, n = 1: E₁ = −13.6 × (2)² / 1² = −13.6 × 4 = **−54.4 eV**.\n   Jaanch: 13.6 × 4 = 54.4 eV ✅.\n\n9. **False ❌.** Bohr ke first postulate ke anusaar stationary orbit mein ghoomte waqt electron **koi EM energy radiate NAHI karta**!\n\n10. (a) **E = −K = −1.51 eV**.\n    (b) **U = 2 E = −3.02 eV**.\n    (c) −13.6 / n² = −1.51 ⟹ n² = 13.6 / 1.51 ≈ 9 ⟹ **n = 3**!\n    Jaanch: −13.6 / 9 = −1.511 eV ✅.\n\n---\n\nAb tum Bohr's Postulates aur Hydrogen atom ke radius, speed aur energy formulas ko pakka samajh chuke ho!\n\n**Agle topic mein:** Hydrogen ke **5 Spectral Series (Lyman se Pfund tak)** aur **de Broglie ne Bohr ka L = nh/2π rule** standing waves se kaise prove kiya — dekhenge!",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. State Bohr's three postulates for the Hydrogen atom.\n2. What is the physical significance of the negative sign in the total energy E_n = −13.6/n² eV of an electron in a Hydrogen atom?\n3. Calculate the radius of the (a) 3rd orbit (n = 3), and (b) 4th orbit (n = 4) of a Hydrogen atom (given a₀ = 0.53 Å).\n4. The total energy of an electron in the first excited state (n = 2) of Hydrogen is −3.4 eV. What are its kinetic energy and potential energy in this state?\n5. Find the ratio of speeds of an electron in the n = 1 and n = 3 orbits of a Hydrogen atom.\n6. Calculate the energy (in eV) of the photon emitted when an electron in Hydrogen jumps from n = 3 (−1.51 eV) to n = 2 (−3.40 eV).\n7. What is the ratio of the radii of the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Bohr orbits of Hydrogen?\n8. Calculate the ground-state (n = 1) total energy of a singly ionised Helium ion He⁺ (Z = 2) using E_n = −13.6 Z²/n² eV.\n9. State whether True or False: According to Bohr's model, an electron continuously radiates electromagnetic energy while revolving in a stationary orbit.\n10. If the kinetic energy of an electron in a Bohr orbit is +1.51 eV, find (a) its total energy, (b) its potential energy, and (c) the orbit number n (for Hydrogen).\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (i) Electron stationary circular orbits mein bina radiation chhode ghoomta hai; (ii) Angular momentum quantised hai: **L = n h / (2π)**; (iii) Jump karne par photon emit/absorb hota hai: **h ν = E_i − E_f**.\n\n2. Negative sign batata hai ki electron nucleus ke electrostatic attraction se **bandha (bound)** hua hai — use atom se poori tarah alag karne ke liye bahar se positive energy deni padegi!\n\n3. (a) r₃ = 0.53 × 3² = 0.53 × 9 = **4.77 Å**.\n   (b) r₄ = 0.53 × 4² = 0.53 × 16 = **8.48 Å**.\n   Jaanch: 0.53 × 9 = 4.77; 0.53 × 16 = 8.48 ✅.\n\n4. **K = −E = +3.4 eV**; **U = 2 E = −6.8 eV**.\n   Jaanch: +3.4 − 6.8 = −3.4 eV ✅.\n\n5. v_n ∝ 1 / n ⟹ **v₁ : v₃ = 3 : 1**.\n\n6. ΔE = E₃ − E₂ = −1.51 − (−3.40) = **1.89 eV**.\n   Jaanch: 3.40 − 1.51 = 1.89 eV ✅.\n\n7. r_n ∝ n² ⟹ r₁ : r₂ : r₃ = 1² : 2² : 3² = **1 : 4 : 9**.\n\n8. Z = 2, n = 1: E₁ = −13.6 × (2)² / 1² = −13.6 × 4 = **−54.4 eV**.\n   Jaanch: 13.6 × 4 = 54.4 eV ✅.\n\n9. **False ❌.** Bohr ke first postulate ke anusaar stationary orbit mein ghoomte waqt electron **koi EM energy radiate NAHI karta**!\n\n10. (a) **E = −K = −1.51 eV**.\n    (b) **U = 2 E = −3.02 eV**.\n    (c) −13.6 / n² = −1.51 ⟹ n² = 13.6 / 1.51 ≈ 9 ⟹ **n = 3**!\n    Jaanch: −13.6 / 9 = −1.511 eV ✅.\n\n---\n\nAb tum Bohr's Postulates aur Hydrogen atom ke radius, speed aur energy formulas ko pakka samajh chuke ho!\n\n**Agle topic mein:** Hydrogen ke **5 Spectral Series (Lyman se Pfund tak)** aur **de Broglie ne Bohr ka L = nh/2π rule** standing waves se kaise prove kiya — dekhenge!"
          }
